-- Generated by `pnpm decisions:seed` from docs/planning/decisions.md (decision 191): the log's
-- entries as decisions, numbered as in the log, active unless a later entry replaces them.
-- Do not edit by hand.
insert into public.decisions
  (number, statement, reason, status, decided_by_name, decided_at, origin, origin_ref)
overriding system value
values
  (203, 'Changes to slice 2.6 after an independent review, before it merged. A decision carries a wording version, one more for each edit; confirming, rejecting or editing a proposal names the wording it was pressed on, and is refused as "changed" if it moved on. A Slack button means the wording first posted, 1, so after an edit in the web app Slack''s Confirm is refused and the person is told, privately, to read it there. A proposal reworded by someone other than the person it names as deciding is in the editor''s name from then on (decided by, and when); its history keeps whose it was. An edit that changes nothing records nothing. `GET /v1/decisions` takes `status=all` and up to 500. A note in the thread never fails an action already saved, and a second press posts a note that was lost. Areas the teammate records are lowercased, and the wiki groups areas whatever their case. Slack tells a person pressing Confirm on a decided proposal that it was already decided', 'The review found that a Slack Confirm could make wording active that the presser never saw, and that a writer could reword a proposal and confirm it with someone else still named as deciding, which is what 195 and 200 closed for recording. Each now has a test. It found no way to act as someone else or on a decision out of reach', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-25T00:00:00Z', 'import', '203')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
